2026-09-02T19:58Z Minh Ha-Duong note blocker 0578 closed — Blocked-by removed.
2026-09-02T23:05Z claude note THIRD ADAPTER LANDED, and the roster's first in-process plugin: jlegewie/beaver-zotero v0.23.3, commit bec71e14, installed from the release beaver.xpi whose sha256 the adapter CHECKS rather than states, in the shipped default configuration with no account. Verdicts: R10-no-egress FAIL, R15-uninstall FAIL, R15-residue PASS, R10-local-by-default and R15-model-cache not-offered, zero not-run. Four verbs absent and each reason is a different finding. query: three surfaces, three different closures -- the MCP endpoint is never mounted because its preference ships false (useMcpServer.ts:1478; MEASURED on a running instance, /connector/ping 200 while /beaver/mcp, /beaver/search and /mcp all 404), ~120 /beaver/* HTTP endpoints are compiled out of the shipped build (useHttpEndpoints.ts:1325, and the string 'Not registering endpoints in production' is IN the shipped bundle), and zotero://beaver carries no query text and returns noContent (protocolHandler.ts:126-140). status: nothing machine-readable, only in-process methods (backgroundExtractor.ts:150-152, documentCache.ts:968-974) and an in-memory atom that is never persisted (embeddingIndex.ts:18-43). pause/resume: TWO background workers and no single control -- the extractor has a real durable pause in a hidden pref, read per tick, re-armed by an observer, in-flight jobs released not lost, job state checkpointed in SQLite; embedding indexing has NO pause and stops only by losing auth, its one control being a rebuild. THREE NEW INTERFACE FINDINGS. (1) derived_state_roots cannot express state written into a file the HOST owns: the target writes extensions.zotero.beaver.* into Zotero's own prefs.js (measured: installedVersion, onboardingWelcomeShown, onboardingWelcomeShownAt, deletionJobs after one no-account launch). Declaring the file as a root claims the host's preferences are the target's and makes R15's uninstall clause demand their deletion; omitting it under-declares. Recorded as a not_derived_state admission, which is that field's documented purpose. (2) The residue sweep loses most of its power on this class: beaver.sqlite sits beside zotero.sqlite and <profile>/beaver beside cookies.sqlite, and residue() exempts by PATH PREFIX, so the only way to stop the host's several hundred files reading as strays is to exempt the host's two directories whole -- which also exempts anywhere inside them the target could stray. No third option exists in the interface and a hand-listed exemption of host filenames is the gate-scope trap. Cost written into each entry rather than left to be inferred from a green; the run compared 1143 created files, which is what says the sweep was not vacuous. (3) A sidecar database is a FILE FAMILY, not a directory, and this exposed a FALSE GREEN in shared layer code: Snapshot.of was os.walk alone, os.walk yields nothing for a regular file, every root of the first two targets is a directory, so the uninstall survivor check returned PASS with three of this target's files on disk. Fixed in assertions.py, pinned by a fixture, and it is what makes the R15 uninstall red visible at all. R10, WITH THE ARENA STATE CONTROLLED. The host application ALONE fails this clause here, so 'Beaver fails R10' is not a finding; the difference is. Controlled A/B, identical profile shape, virgin in both, same 90s window, only the artifact differing: with-plugin 430 name lookups and 0 off-machine, host-only 426 and 0 -- +4, and under isolation neither cell can say to whom, because every name dies at the loopback stub resolver. The host-only cell reproduces the lane lead's independently measured 426 TO THE DIGIT. So a second, route-intact observation was taken (bench/r10_target_destinations.py, an observation carried beside the verdict, never one): destinations present with the plugin and absent without it are exactly the four addresses objects.githubusercontent.com resolves to plus lb-fra.github.com -- the add-on's own update_url, egress CAUSED by the target and PERFORMED by its host -- and two Cloudflare /24s that the Supabase project the shipped bundle is compiled against resolves to (consistent with, not proof of, given anycast). What is ABSENT is half the finding: api.beaverapp.ai's address never appears, matching the source gate where getAuthHeaders throws before fetch with no session (apiService.ts:281-290). NOT-RUN FOR WANT OF CREDENTIALS, stated rather than scored: whether the effective embedder is local (R10's other clause), whether the mode selected is the mode served (R33), and whether retrieval is local at all -- semantic search reads vectors from local SQLite but fetches the QUERY embedding from the backend (semanticSearchService.ts:71) and the local metadata path is fail-closed on an empty library scope until an authenticated profile loads (profile.ts:96-101,116-119). The plugin does name a model locally, voyage-3-int8-512 (embeddingIndexer.ts:195), but it is a client-side label for vectors the backend computed, so reporting it as the embedder in effect would be the adapter scoring a result. TWO LIFECYCLE DEFECTS MET RATHER THAN IMAGINED. The host's launcher is a shell script that runs the real binary as a CHILD, so Popen.terminate killed the script and orphaned two instances that outlived their lifecycle still holding their databases open; the lifecycle now signals the process GROUP. And piping the host's stdout with no reader can block it at 64 KB, so the output is drained and its tail reported as evidence. OPEN QUESTION, reported rather than attributed: the layer's own subject arm counts 60 name lookups where the matched raw launch counts 430. Three hypotheses tested by intervention and all three failed -- the unread pipe (60 before and after draining), a shorter window (430 at 78s as at 90s), a detached session (430 under setsid) -- and a timestamped trace puts all 430 inside the first 70 seconds, so no shutdown burst explains it. The one experiment that would settle it is named in the results README. Sixteen control arms were planted against the committed tree and all sixteen went red. Also confirmed for the lead: this target does NOT read the library over Zotero's local HTTP API; it holds Zotero's own data layer in-process (Zotero.DBConnection at hooks.ts:242, Zotero.DataDirectory at externalFiles.ts:118, quickSearchItems in-process), so query_transport is being asked to describe something that is not a transport at all. Three targets now run through one layer -- available() lists beaver, zotero-mcp and zoteus -- and the layer still holds no target's name.

--- body ---
## Context

The ratified target-neutral harness includes Beaver as a real fifth target.
Its plugin is AGPL-3.0 and can be pinned and inspected; its hosted backend is an
external runtime dependency. Beaver is expected to fail R10 where its normal
configuration attempts disclosed remote processing. The deterministic
egressing stub in ticket 0578 remains the assertion's fail-control; Beaver is
not shaped into a fixture.

## Actions

1. Pin the tested Beaver plugin revision and document the normal configuration.
2. Declare derived state, UI/query access, lifecycle, default configuration and
   unsupported interface verbs without compensating for target behavior.
3. Run applicable assertions, including R10 with network-attempt observation.
4. Record unavailable service or permitted credentials as not-run, never pass,
   and assess other clauses independently of the expected R10 result.

## Exit criteria

- [x] pinned AGPL Beaver plugin revision and recorded normal configuration
- [x] adapter passes ticket 0578's declaration-only contract checks
- [x] R10 reports the observed result without a specially failing configuration
- [ ] unavailable hosted service or credentials produce not-run — DELIBERATELY LEFT
      OPEN. The run reached zero not-run, and that is not the criterion being met
      quietly. The clauses credentials would have unblocked (R10's local-by-default,
      R33's mode-served) are unreachable on this target BY DECLARATION, because the
      default configuration exposes no query and no status surface at all — a
      stronger statement than not-run, and the `unsupported` reason carries the
      credential fact beside it. Nothing was scored as a pass for want of an
      account. The author's call whether that satisfies the line as written.
- [x] every other applicable requirement is assessed independently
- [x] `make check` and `erg check tickets/` pass
